module Core

### ObjectHacker's weak observation of a Roamed entity — a NON-PINNING handle minted by
### `Roamed[T].watch()`. It does NOT keep the entity alive; after the entity dies it survives as a
### tombstone view so `is_alive()`/`is_destroyed()` stay answerable without dangling. "Weak" is an
### internal property of the substrate (RoamController's weak/tombstone layer) — users of ObjectHacker
### just hold a `Watching` and ask whether the object is still there; they never see a weak-reference
### concept. Holds only the controller address (the weak edge); `0` = the absent observation.
### :typeparam T: The observed entity type.
###
### NOTE (experiment): balanced copy semantics (observe-on-copy, like `Witnessed[T, P].share`) are a
### follow-up. `Watching` currently carries only a scalar address (no hand-written `store`), so a
### return is a bitwise MOVE — mint (`watch`) observes once, the single live handle's `destroy`
### unobserves once. Do not COPY a `Watching` yet (a bitwise copy would unbalance the weak count).
record Watching[T]
needs T is EntityType
  ### The observed entity's {RoamController} address — the weak edge. `0` for the absent observation.
  secret ctrl: Address

### Whether the observed entity is still alive. Safe after the entity's death (reads the tombstone's
### `dead` flag, never the freed entity data). :returns: `true` until the entity has been destroyed.
routine Watching[T].is_alive() -> Bool
  danger
    if me.ctrl == 0_addr
      return false
    return Hijacked[RoamController[T]](from: me.ctrl).as_entity().is_alive()

### Whether the observed entity has been destroyed (by either free path). :returns: `true` once gone.
routine Watching[T].is_destroyed() -> Bool
  danger
    if me.ctrl == 0_addr
      return true
    return Hijacked[RoamController[T]](from: me.ctrl).as_entity().is_destroyed()

### Releases the weak observation. If this was the last observer of an already-dead (tombstoned)
### controller, the controller struct is finally freed. Called at scope exit like any owned handle.
@override
dangerous routine Watching[T].destroy()
  if me.ctrl != 0_addr
    Hijacked[RoamController[T]](from: me.ctrl).as_entity().unobserve()
  return
